module

public import TauCeti.Algebra.Lie.UniversalEnveloping.Kostant.RootSubgroup.Scheme.ToralClosure.NumberedSymmetry
public import TauCeti.CategoryTheory.Aut.Basic
public import TauCeti.LinearAlgebra.RootSystem.GeckConstruction.PinnedSymmetry
public import TauCeti.LinearAlgebra.RootSystem.SimplyConnectedRootDatum.GeckLattice.GroupScheme

/-!
# The graph automorphism of the pinned Geck group scheme

`TauCeti.DynkinType.geckGroupScheme` is the explicit affine group scheme over `ℤ` attached to a
valid Dynkin type: the closed subgroup scheme of `GLₙ` generated by the divided-power exponential
root subgroups of the Bourbaki-numbered Chevalley generators together with the weight torus of the
Geck coordinate lattice. A symmetry of the Bourbaki-numbered Cartan matrix permutes those
generators, and this file turns it into an automorphism of the carrier.

Everything needed is already pinned. On the representation side,
`TauCeti.DynkinType.geckDiagramModuleEquiv` is the coordinate permutation of Geck's module induced
by a node permutation `σ`; it preserves the integral coordinate lattice, it intertwines the
numbered raising and lowering generators with the ones numbered by `σ`, and it permutes the Geck
weights contragrediently. On the group-scheme side,
`TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantToralNumberedSymmetryIso` converts exactly that data
into an automorphism of a Kostant toral closure. What this file supplies is the missing bridge
between them and the resulting named automorphism of the pinned carrier with its pinning equations.

Writing `γ` for the automorphism, `xᵢ` for the root subgroup of the numbered generator `i` and
`T` for the represented weight torus, those equations are

```text
γ ∘ xᵢ = x_{σ i},        γ ∘ T = T ∘ relabel σ⁻¹,
```

with `σ` acting on the raising and lowering halves of the generator index by the same node
permutation. The first is the expected pinning equation for a graph automorphism, stated on the
simple root subgroups where a pinning normalizes the parameter. The second says that `γ` normalizes
the torus and acts on its cocharacters by the node permutation.

The construction is multiplicative in the node permutation, and
`TauCeti.DynkinType.geckDiagramAutHom` records that as a homomorphism out of the symmetry group of
the Cartan matrix. That is what turns a relation satisfied by a permutation into the same relation
for the automorphism it induces: the order-two symmetries of `Aₙ`, `Dₙ` and `E₆` give `γ ^ 2 = 1`
and the triality of `D₄` gives `γ ^ 3 = 1`, with no separate argument in each case.

Two limitations are worth stating. The Geck weights span the root lattice rather than, in general,
the full character lattice, so this carrier is the adjoint form and not yet the simply connected one
a finite group of Lie type is built from; nothing below asserts that it is reductive, that its torus
is maximal, or that `γ` is an automorphism of any finite group. And `γ` is built from the chosen
coordinate permutation rather than characterized by its pinning equations: uniqueness is the
isomorphism theorem for pinned groups, which is not proved here.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.DynkinType.geckDiagramAut`: the induced automorphism of the pinned Geck carrier.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.geckDiagramAutHom`: the same construction as a homomorphism out of the
  symmetry group of the Bourbaki-numbered Cartan matrix.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.DynkinType.geckRootSubgroup_comp_geckDiagramAut_hom` and its inverse and iterated
  counterparts: the pinning equation `γ ∘ xᵢ = x_{σ i}` on the numbered root subgroups.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.geckWeightTorus_comp_geckDiagramAut_hom` and its inverse counterpart: the
  automorphism normalizes the represented weight torus and acts on it by relabelling.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.geckDiagramAut_one` and `TauCeti.DynkinType.geckDiagramAut_mul`: the
  construction is a monoid homomorphism in the node permutation.
* `TauCeti.DynkinType.geckDiagramAut_pow_eq_one`: a node permutation of finite order induces an
  automorphism satisfying the same relation.

## References

* M. Geck, *On the construction of semisimple Lie algebras and Chevalley groups*,
  Proc. Amer. Math. Soc. **145** (2017), 3233--3247.
* R. W. Carter, *Finite Groups of Lie Type: Conjugacy Classes and Complex Characters*, §1.15.
* J. E. Humphreys, *Linear Algebraic Groups*, §27.
* J. C. Jantzen, *Representations of Algebraic Groups*, II.1.

This is the pinned instance of the "pinnings" target of Layer 9 of
`TauCetiRoadmap/ReductiveGroups/README.md`, which asks that a pinning be the data making "the"
graph automorphism well defined. Its consumer is milestone L1 of
`TauCetiRoadmap/CFSGStatement/README.md`, whose graph-twisted Steinberg maps are `γ ∘ Frob_q` for
`γ` the automorphism attached to `Fin.revPerm` on `Aₙ`, to `Equiv.swap (n - 2) (n - 1)` on `Dₙ`, to
`Equiv.swap 0 5 * Equiv.swap 2 4` on `E₆` and to the three-cycle `(0 2 3)` on `D₄`, and whose
completion evidence is "the simple-root-subgroup equations and the order relations are proved".
-/

public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory

namespace TauCeti.DynkinType

noncomputable section

-- Matrices form a Lie ring through their commutator, which is how Geck's construction reads them.
attribute [local instance 100] LieRing.ofAssociativeRing

attribute [local instance] TauCeti.moduleNNRat

-- Match tensor products to the `ℤ`-algebra structure used by scalar extension.
attribute [local instance high] Algebra.toModule

variable {t : DynkinType} (ht : t.Valid) {sigma tau : Equiv.Perm (Fin t.rank)}

/-! ## The coordinate basis permutation -/

/-- The permutation of the finite-ordinal Geck coordinate basis induced by a symmetry of the
Bourbaki-numbered Dynkin diagram. It is `TauCeti.DynkinType.geckDiagramIndexEquiv` read through the
`Fintype.equivFin` ordering of the Geck index. -/
private def geckDiagramBasisPerm (hsigma : sigma ∈ t.diagramSymmetry) :
    Equiv.Perm (Fin (t.geckDim ht)) :=
  (Fintype.equivFin (t.GeckIndex ht)).permCongr (t.geckDiagramIndexEquiv ht hsigma)

/-- The coordinate basis permutation acts by transporting the Geck-index permutation along the
`Fintype.equivFin` ordering. -/
@[simp]
private theorem geckDiagramBasisPerm_apply (hsigma : sigma ∈ t.diagramSymmetry)
    (i : Fin (t.geckDim ht)) :
    t.geckDiagramBasisPerm ht hsigma i =
      Fintype.equivFin (t.GeckIndex ht)
        (t.geckDiagramIndexEquiv ht hsigma ((Fintype.equivFin (t.GeckIndex ht)).symm i)) :=
  (rfl)

/-- **The pinned module symmetry permutes the finite-ordinal coordinate basis.** This is the
basis-permutation hypothesis of the Kostant toral-closure symmetry construction. -/
private theorem geckDiagramModuleEquiv_coe_geckCoordinateBasisFin
    (hsigma : sigma ∈ t.diagramSymmetry)
    (i : Fin (t.geckDim ht)) :
    t.geckDiagramModuleEquiv ht hsigma
        ((t.geckCoordinateBasisFin ht i : (t.geckCoordinateLattice ht).toAddSubgroup) :
          t.GeckIndex ht → ℚ) =
      ((t.geckCoordinateBasisFin ht (t.geckDiagramBasisPerm ht hsigma i) :
        (t.geckCoordinateLattice ht).toAddSubgroup) : t.GeckIndex ht → ℚ) := by
  rw [coe_geckCoordinateBasisFin, geckDiagramModuleEquiv_single, coe_geckCoordinateBasisFin,
    geckDiagramBasisPerm_apply, Equiv.symm_apply_apply]

/-- **The finite-ordinal Geck weights are equivariant** for the coordinate basis permutation and
the node permutation. This is the weight hypothesis of the Kostant toral-closure symmetry
construction. -/
private theorem geckWeightFin_geckDiagramBasisPerm (hsigma : sigma ∈ t.diagramSymmetry)
    (i : Fin (t.geckDim ht)) (k : Fin t.rank) :
    t.geckWeightFin ht (t.geckDiagramBasisPerm ht hsigma i) (sigma k) =
      t.geckWeightFin ht i k := by
  simp only [geckWeightFin, geckDiagramBasisPerm_apply, Equiv.symm_apply_apply]
  exact t.geckWeight_geckDiagramIndexEquiv ht hsigma _ k

/-! ## The automorphism of the carrier -/

/-- The automorphism of the Kostant toral closure of the pinned Geck data induced by a diagram
symmetry. This is the implementation of `TauCeti.DynkinType.geckDiagramAut`; consumers use the
named Geck API and its pinning equations. -/
private def geckToralDiagramIso (hsigma : sigma ∈ t.diagramSymmetry) :
    Aut (TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantToralGroupScheme
      (t.lieBasis ht).rootGenerator (t.lieBasis ht).h (t.geckRepresentation ht)
      (t.geckCoordinateLattice ht).toAddSubgroup
      (t.geckRepresentation_kostantForm_mem_geckCoordinateLattice ht)
      (t.isNilpotent_geckRepresentation_rootGenerator ht)
      (t.geckCoordinateBasisFin ht) (t.geckWeightFin ht)) :=
  TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantToralNumberedSymmetryIso
    (t.lieBasis ht).rootGenerator (t.lieBasis ht).h (t.geckRepresentation ht)
    (t.geckCoordinateLattice ht).toAddSubgroup
    (t.geckRepresentation_kostantForm_mem_geckCoordinateLattice ht)
    (t.isNilpotent_geckRepresentation_rootGenerator ht)
    (t.geckCoordinateBasisFin ht) (t.geckWeightFin ht)
    ⇑(diagramRootGeneratorPerm sigma) (t.geckDiagramModuleEquiv ht hsigma)
    (fun v => t.geckDiagramModuleEquiv_mem_geckCoordinateLattice_iff ht hsigma v)
    (fun i v => by
      simpa only [_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι_apply] using
        t.geckDiagramModuleEquiv_geckRepresentation_rootGenerator ht hsigma i v)
    (diagramRootGeneratorPerm sigma).surjective
    (t.geckDiagramBasisPerm ht hsigma)
    (fun i => t.geckDiagramModuleEquiv_coe_geckCoordinateBasisFin ht hsigma i)
    sigma
    (fun i k => t.geckWeightFin_geckDiagramBasisPerm ht hsigma i k)

/-- **The graph automorphism of the pinned Geck carrier attached to a symmetry of the
Bourbaki-numbered Cartan matrix.** It permutes the numbered root subgroups by the node permutation
and normalizes the represented weight torus. -/
def geckDiagramAut (hsigma : sigma ∈ t.diagramSymmetry) : Aut (t.geckGroupScheme ht) :=
  Aut.autMulEquivOfIso (eqToIso (t.geckGroupScheme_def ht)).symm
    (geckToralDiagramIso ht hsigma)

/-- The forward morphism of the graph automorphism, read on the Kostant toral closure. The name
records the projected field, since `TauCeti.DynkinType.geckDiagramAut_inv` below is about the
automorphism attached to the inverse node permutation. -/
private theorem hom_geckDiagramAut (hsigma : sigma ∈ t.diagramSymmetry) :
    (t.geckDiagramAut ht hsigma).hom =
      eqToHom (t.geckGroupScheme_def ht) ≫ (geckToralDiagramIso ht hsigma).hom ≫
        eqToHom (t.geckGroupScheme_def ht).symm := (rfl)

/-- The inverse morphism of the graph automorphism, read on the Kostant toral closure. -/
private theorem inv_geckDiagramAut (hsigma : sigma ∈ t.diagramSymmetry) :
    (t.geckDiagramAut ht hsigma).inv =
      eqToHom (t.geckGroupScheme_def ht) ≫ (geckToralDiagramIso ht hsigma).inv ≫
        eqToHom (t.geckGroupScheme_def ht).symm := (rfl)

/-! ## The pinning equations -/

/-- **The graph automorphism carries the `i`th numbered root subgroup to the one numbered by the
permuted index**, without changing its additive parameter. This is the expected pinning equation. -/
@[simp]
theorem geckRootSubgroup_comp_geckDiagramAut_hom (hsigma : sigma ∈ t.diagramSymmetry)
    (i : Fin t.rank ⊕ Fin t.rank) :
    t.geckRootSubgroup ht i ≫ (t.geckDiagramAut ht hsigma).hom =
      t.geckRootSubgroup ht (diagramRootGeneratorPerm sigma i) := by
  rw [geckRootSubgroup_def, geckRootSubgroup_def, hom_geckDiagramAut, geckToralDiagramIso]
  simp only [Category.assoc, eqToHom_trans_assoc, eqToHom_refl, Category.id_comp]
  rw [← Category.assoc,
    TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantRootSubgroupToToral_comp_numberedSymmetryIso_hom]

/-- The inverse graph automorphism carries the root subgroup numbered by the permuted index back to
the `i`th one. -/
@[simp]
theorem geckRootSubgroup_comp_geckDiagramAut_inv (hsigma : sigma ∈ t.diagramSymmetry)
    (i : Fin t.rank ⊕ Fin t.rank) :
    t.geckRootSubgroup ht (diagramRootGeneratorPerm sigma i) ≫
        (t.geckDiagramAut ht hsigma).inv =
      t.geckRootSubgroup ht i := by
  rw [← geckRootSubgroup_comp_geckDiagramAut_hom ht hsigma i, Category.assoc,
    (t.geckDiagramAut ht hsigma).hom_inv_id, Category.comp_id]

/-- **The graph automorphism normalizes the represented weight torus**, acting on it by the
relabelling attached to the inverse node permutation. -/
@[simp]
theorem geckWeightTorus_comp_geckDiagramAut_hom (hsigma : sigma ∈ t.diagramSymmetry) :
    t.geckWeightTorus ht ≫ (t.geckDiagramAut ht hsigma).hom =
      SplitTorus.relabel ℤ sigma⁻¹ ≫ t.geckWeightTorus ht := by
  rw [geckWeightTorus_def, hom_geckDiagramAut, geckToralDiagramIso]
  simp only [Category.assoc, eqToHom_trans_assoc, eqToHom_refl, Category.id_comp]
  rw [← Category.assoc,
    TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantWeightTorusToToral_comp_numberedSymmetryIso_hom,
    Category.assoc]

/-- The inverse graph automorphism acts on the represented weight torus by the relabelling attached
to the node permutation itself. -/
@[simp]
theorem geckWeightTorus_comp_geckDiagramAut_inv (hsigma : sigma ∈ t.diagramSymmetry) :
    t.geckWeightTorus ht ≫ (t.geckDiagramAut ht hsigma).inv =
      SplitTorus.relabel ℤ sigma ≫ t.geckWeightTorus ht := by
  rw [geckWeightTorus_def, inv_geckDiagramAut, geckToralDiagramIso]
  simp only [Category.assoc, eqToHom_trans_assoc, eqToHom_refl, Category.id_comp]
  rw [← Category.assoc,
    TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantWeightTorusToToral_comp_numberedSymmetryIso_inv,
    Category.assoc]

/-! ## Multiplicativity -/

/-- The implementation automorphism attached to the identity node permutation is the identity. -/
private theorem geckToralDiagramIso_one :
    geckToralDiagramIso ht t.diagramSymmetry.one_mem = 1 := by
  apply Iso.ext
  refine TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantToralGroupScheme_hom_ext
    (t.lieBasis ht).rootGenerator (t.lieBasis ht).h (t.geckRepresentation ht)
    (t.geckCoordinateLattice ht).toAddSubgroup
    (t.geckRepresentation_kostantForm_mem_geckCoordinateLattice ht)
    (t.isNilpotent_geckRepresentation_rootGenerator ht)
    (t.geckCoordinateBasisFin ht) (t.geckWeightFin ht) _ _ (fun i => ?_) ?_
  · rw [geckToralDiagramIso,
      TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantRootSubgroupToToral_comp_numberedSymmetryIso_hom,
      diagramRootGeneratorPerm_one, Equiv.Perm.coe_one, id_eq]
    -- the identity of `Aut` is definitionally `Iso.refl`, exposed here by `change`
    change _ = _ ≫ (Iso.refl _).hom
    rw [Iso.refl_hom, Category.comp_id]
  · rw [geckToralDiagramIso,
      TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantWeightTorusToToral_comp_numberedSymmetryIso_hom,
      inv_one, SplitTorus.relabel_one, Category.id_comp]
    change _ = _ ≫ (Iso.refl _).hom
    rw [Iso.refl_hom, Category.comp_id]

/-- The implementation automorphism is multiplicative in the node permutation. -/
private theorem geckToralDiagramIso_mul (hsigma : sigma ∈ t.diagramSymmetry)
    (htau : tau ∈ t.diagramSymmetry) :
    geckToralDiagramIso ht (t.diagramSymmetry.mul_mem hsigma htau) =
      geckToralDiagramIso ht hsigma * geckToralDiagramIso ht htau := by
  apply Iso.ext
  refine TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantToralGroupScheme_hom_ext
    (t.lieBasis ht).rootGenerator (t.lieBasis ht).h (t.geckRepresentation ht)
    (t.geckCoordinateLattice ht).toAddSubgroup
    (t.geckRepresentation_kostantForm_mem_geckCoordinateLattice ht)
    (t.isNilpotent_geckRepresentation_rootGenerator ht)
    (t.geckCoordinateBasisFin ht) (t.geckWeightFin ht) _ _ (fun i => ?_) ?_
  · rw [geckToralDiagramIso,
      TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantRootSubgroupToToral_comp_numberedSymmetryIso_hom]
    -- `Aut` multiplication is reverse categorical composition, exposed here at the hom level
    change _ = _ ≫ (geckToralDiagramIso ht htau).hom ≫ (geckToralDiagramIso ht hsigma).hom
    rw [← Category.assoc, geckToralDiagramIso, geckToralDiagramIso,
      TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantRootSubgroupToToral_comp_numberedSymmetryIso_hom,
      TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantRootSubgroupToToral_comp_numberedSymmetryIso_hom,
      diagramRootGeneratorPerm_mul, Equiv.Perm.mul_apply]
  · rw [geckToralDiagramIso,
      TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantWeightTorusToToral_comp_numberedSymmetryIso_hom]
    change _ = _ ≫ (geckToralDiagramIso ht htau).hom ≫ (geckToralDiagramIso ht hsigma).hom
    rw [← Category.assoc, geckToralDiagramIso, geckToralDiagramIso,
      TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantWeightTorusToToral_comp_numberedSymmetryIso_hom,
      Category.assoc,
      TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.kostantWeightTorusToToral_comp_numberedSymmetryIso_hom,
      ← Category.assoc, SplitTorus.relabel_comp, mul_inv_rev]

/-- The identity node permutation induces the identity automorphism of the carrier. -/
@[simp]
theorem geckDiagramAut_one : t.geckDiagramAut ht t.diagramSymmetry.one_mem = 1 := by
  rw [geckDiagramAut, geckToralDiagramIso_one, map_one]

/-- The construction is multiplicative in the node permutation. -/
@[simp]
theorem geckDiagramAut_mul (hsigma : sigma ∈ t.diagramSymmetry)
    (htau : tau ∈ t.diagramSymmetry) :
    t.geckDiagramAut ht (t.diagramSymmetry.mul_mem hsigma htau) =
      t.geckDiagramAut ht hsigma * t.geckDiagramAut ht htau := by
  rw [geckDiagramAut, geckDiagramAut, geckDiagramAut, geckToralDiagramIso_mul, map_mul]

/-- **The graph automorphisms of the pinned Geck carrier, as a homomorphism** out of the symmetry
group of the Bourbaki-numbered Cartan matrix. This is what converts a relation satisfied by a node
permutation into the same relation for the automorphism it induces. -/
def geckDiagramAutHom : t.diagramSymmetry →* Aut (t.geckGroupScheme ht) where
  toFun g := t.geckDiagramAut ht g.2
  map_one' := t.geckDiagramAut_one ht
  map_mul' g₁ g₂ := t.geckDiagramAut_mul ht g₁.2 g₂.2

/-- The homomorphism out of the symmetry group evaluates to the named graph automorphism. -/
@[simp]
theorem geckDiagramAutHom_apply (g : t.diagramSymmetry) :
    t.geckDiagramAutHom ht g = t.geckDiagramAut ht g.2 :=
  (rfl)

/-- A node permutation equal to the identity induces the identity automorphism. The membership
proof is irrelevant, so this is `TauCeti.DynkinType.geckDiagramAut_one` with the permutation
allowed to be any expression equal to `1`. -/
private theorem geckDiagramAut_eq_one {s : Equiv.Perm (Fin t.rank)}
    (hs : s ∈ t.diagramSymmetry) (h : s = 1) : t.geckDiagramAut ht hs = 1 := by
  subst h
  exact t.geckDiagramAut_one ht

/-- The inverse node permutation induces the inverse automorphism. -/
@[simp]
theorem geckDiagramAut_inv (hsigma : sigma ∈ t.diagramSymmetry) :
    t.geckDiagramAut ht (t.diagramSymmetry.inv_mem hsigma) = (t.geckDiagramAut ht hsigma)⁻¹ := by
  refine (inv_eq_of_mul_eq_one_left ?_).symm
  rw [← geckDiagramAut_mul]
  exact t.geckDiagramAut_eq_one ht _ (inv_mul_cancel sigma)

/-- **A node permutation of finite order induces an automorphism satisfying the same relation.**
This is the source of `γ ^ 2 = 1` for the order-two diagram symmetries of `Aₙ`, `Dₙ` and `E₆`, and
of `γ ^ 3 = 1` for the triality of `D₄`. -/
theorem geckDiagramAut_pow_eq_one (hsigma : sigma ∈ t.diagramSymmetry) {n : ℕ}
    (hn : sigma ^ n = 1) : t.geckDiagramAut ht hsigma ^ n = 1 := by
  have h : (⟨sigma, hsigma⟩ : t.diagramSymmetry) ^ n = 1 := Subtype.ext (by simpa using hn)
  calc t.geckDiagramAut ht hsigma ^ n = t.geckDiagramAutHom ht (⟨sigma, hsigma⟩ ^ n) := by
        rw [map_pow, geckDiagramAutHom_apply]
    _ = 1 := by rw [h, map_one]

/-- Iterating the graph automorphism carries the `i`th numbered root subgroup to the one numbered
by the corresponding power of the node permutation. -/
@[simp]
theorem geckRootSubgroup_comp_geckDiagramAut_pow_hom (hsigma : sigma ∈ t.diagramSymmetry)
    (m : ℕ) (i : Fin t.rank ⊕ Fin t.rank) :
    t.geckRootSubgroup ht i ≫ ((t.geckDiagramAut ht hsigma) ^ m).hom =
      t.geckRootSubgroup ht (diagramRootGeneratorPerm (sigma ^ m) i) := by
  rw [diagramRootGeneratorPerm_pow, Equiv.Perm.coe_pow]
  exact TauCeti.CategoryTheory.comp_aut_pow_hom_of_comp (t.geckDiagramAut ht hsigma)
    (t.geckRootSubgroup ht) ⇑(diagramRootGeneratorPerm sigma)
    (fun i => t.geckRootSubgroup_comp_geckDiagramAut_hom ht hsigma i) m i

end

end TauCeti.DynkinType
